//! Domain B: the consequence-mass allocation input model (`case_studies`,
//! `generalization`), generated by `generator.py` from `ontology/
//! {cmca-rdf.ttl,generalization.ttl}`. Named `consequence_mass` (not `cmca`)
//! because this module is only half of what `bcinr-cmca` means by "CMCA"
//! (Covariance Monitoring and Calibration Assessment, per this crate's own
//! `lib.rs` doc) -- the other half is `generated::stability_profile`, the
//! gain-matrix stability certificate. `~/mfw`'s own, separately-maintained
//! ontology docs use the identical `cmca:` RDF vocabulary for this same
//! consequence-mass-allocation scheme under the bare name "CMCA", which is
//! exactly the collision this module's name is scoped to avoid at the Rust
//! source level.
pub mod case_studies;
pub mod generalization;
